Error: Jet.TypestateWrongState: `ship` needs `Order.Confirmed`, but `order` is `Order.Draft`
  --> Tests/UI/Typestate/typestate_parameter_carries_state.jet:27:64
    |
 27 | ship_draft_param: fn(order: ^^Order.Draft) -> String { "{order.ship().id}" }
    |                                                                ^^^^
 Why: Typestate: `ship` takes only `Order.Confirmed`; calling it with `Order` in another state is the out-of-order bug the state list rules out
 Fix: Moves from `Order.Draft`: `confirm`, `cancel`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.TypestateWrongState

